{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdnYUmuCYnKNpgeyzvWLB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SwnhK5eJUngYq84GmmzqN3","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/jerodw/Work/AgenticProgramming/level-five/prompts/planner.md","old_string":"The workflow definition stops some stages from creating files under some\npaths: the implementer may not create anything under tests/, because new\nvalidation is the tester's work. A stage_exceptions entry lifts one of\nthose restrictions for one story, which is what a story whose own\ndeliverable is a test suite needs.","new_string":"Every likely_file_changes entry names the workflow stage expected to make\nthat change. The workflow this repository runs defines exactly these\nstages, and a plan naming any other one is a planning error:\n\n{{workflow_stages}}\n\nThe scope you write is not the only boundary. These paths are blocked by\nrules/execution-rules.json for every stage of every story, enforced by the\nharness rather than by a story's own do_not_modify list:\n\n{{blocked_paths}}\n\nThe workflow definition also stops some stages from creating files under\nsome paths, because the work belongs to a later stage:\n\n{{stage_create_restrictions}}\n\nA stage_exceptions entry lifts one of those restrictions for one story,\nwhich is what a story whose own deliverable is a test suite needs."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_read_input_tokens":47697,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":396},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c3fc9de-acc0-4d44-bf99-2824655b2225","uuid":"304d9e61-540b-49e2-bd71-1aa89e27d7be","timestamp":"2026-08-07T01:46:09.040Z","request_id":"req_011CdnYUjd2U2wqhiZc8kQvh"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwnhK5eJUngYq84GmmzqN3","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/jerodw/Work/AgenticProgramming/level-five/prompts/planner.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c3fc9de-acc0-4d44-bf99-2824655b2225","uuid":"8d37bb48-68df-45a9-bd46-9015b0143677","timestamp":"2026-08-07T01:46:09.159Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/jerodw/Work/AgenticProgramming/level-five/prompts/planner.md","oldString":"The workflow definition stops some stages from creating files under some\npaths: the implementer may not create anything under tests/, because new\nvalidation is the tester's work. A stage_exceptions entry lifts one of\nthose restrictions for one story, which is what a story whose own\ndeliverable is a test suite needs.","newString":"Every likely_file_changes entry names the workflow stage expected to make\nthat change. The workflow this repository runs defines exactly these\nstages, and a plan naming any other one is a planning error:\n\n{{workflow_stages}}\n\nThe scope you write is not the only boundary. These paths are blocked by\nrules/execution-rules.json for every stage of every story, enforced by the\nharness rather than by a story's own do_not_modify list:\n\n{{blocked_paths}}\n\nThe workflow definition also stops some stages from creating files under\nsome paths, because the work belongs to a later stage:\n\n{{stage_create_restrictions}}\n\nA stage_exceptions entry lifts one of those restrictions for one story,\nwhich is what a story whose own deliverable is a test suite needs.","originalFile":"You are the story planner for the l5 agentic harness.\n\n[Role Layer]\nYour responsibility is to turn a story request into an execution contract\nthe rest of the harness can execute without renegotiating scope, intent,\nor sequence. Planning at this level is interactive: work with the\ndeveloper until the story is clear, then write the approved artifact.\n\nYour responsibilities are to:\n- decompose the requested story into tasks,\n- define explicit scope boundaries (what to modify, what not to modify),\n- generate specific, evaluable acceptance criteria,\n- identify verification requirements, and\n- preserve repository conventions.\n\nDo not:\n- implement code,\n- begin planning implementation details before the request is clear,\n- expand the story beyond a single bounded change, or\n- write the story artifact before the developer approves the plan.\n\n[Process]\n1. Read .harness/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and the standards in .harness/standards/.\n2. Ask the developer any questions required to remove important\n   ambiguity. Ask about decisions that are expensive or hard to reverse;\n   apply sensible defaults to cheap, reversible ones and say you did.\n3. Present the draft plan and iterate until the developer approves it.\n4. Determine the next story number by listing .harness/stories/ and write\n   the approved artifact there as story-NNN.yaml.\n\n[Story artifact format]\nThe contract is schemas/story.schema.json, injected below. It says which\nsections and fields a story must carry; l5-run parses and validates the\nartifact against that same file before a run starts, so a story that does\nnot satisfy it is refused at pre-flight.\n\n{{story_schema}}\n\nThe story dialect is not JSON and it is not YAML. The schema above says\nwhat must be present; the skeleton below is an illustration of how to\nwrite it — indentation, block scalars, and dash-prefixed items. Read the\nschema for the contract and the skeleton for the shape.\n\n\tstory:\n\t  id: story-NNN\n\t  title: <short title>\n\t  description: |\n\t    <what this story adds or changes, and why>\n\n\ttasks:\n\t  - <bounded task>\n\t  - <bounded task>\n\n\tacceptance_criteria:\n\t  - <specific, evaluable condition>\n\t  - <specific, evaluable condition>\n\n\ttechnical_plan:\n\t  implementation_steps:\n\t    - <step>\n\t  likely_file_changes:\n\t    - file: <path>\n\t      stage: <the workflow stage expected to change it>\n\t      reason: <why>\n\n\tscope:\n\t  modify:\n\t    - <path or area>\n\t  do_not_modify:\n\t    - <path or area>\n\n\tverification_requirements:\n\t  - <what the verifier must confirm>\n\n\tconstraints:\n\t  - <behavior that must be preserved>\n\nThe workflow definition stops some stages from creating files under some\npaths: the implementer may not create anything under tests/, because new\nvalidation is the tester's work. A stage_exceptions entry lifts one of\nthose restrictions for one story, which is what a story whose own\ndeliverable is a test suite needs.\n\nDo not add one without asking the developer first. The stage must be a\nstage the workflow defines, and the create path must be one that stage\nis actually restricted from creating. If either is wrong, l5-run refuses\nto run the story at all. Use reason to say why this story needs the\nrestriction lifted:\n\n\tstage_exceptions:\n\t  - stage: <stage the exception applies to>\n\t    create: <path prefix that stage is normally not allowed to create under>\n\t    reason: <why this story needs the restriction lifted>\n\nAfter writing the artifact, tell the developer the story id and how to\nexecute it: scripts/l5-run <story-id>.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":75,"oldLines":12,"newStart":75,"newLines":26,"lines":["   constraints:","     - <behavior that must be preserved>"," ","-The workflow definition stops some stages from creating files under some","-paths: the implementer may not create anything under tests/, because new","-validation is the tester's work. A stage_exceptions entry lifts one of","-those restrictions for one story, which is what a story whose own","-deliverable is a test suite needs.","+Every likely_file_changes entry names the workflow stage expected to make","+that change. The workflow this repository runs defines exactly these","+stages, and a plan naming any other one is a planning error:"," ","+{{workflow_stages}}","+","+The scope you write is not the only boundary. These paths are blocked by","+rules/execution-rules.json for every stage of every story, enforced by the","+harness rather than by a story's own do_not_modify list:","+","+{{blocked_paths}}","+","+The workflow definition also stops some stages from creating files under","+some paths, because the work belongs to a later stage:","+","+{{stage_create_restrictions}}","+","+A stage_exceptions entry lifts one of those restrictions for one story,","+which is what a story whose own deliverable is a test suite needs.","+"," Do not add one without asking the developer first. The stage must be a"," stage the workflow defines, and the create path must be one that stage"," is actually restricted from creating. If either is wrong, l5-run refuses"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
