cked by\nrules/execution-rules.json for every stage of every story, enforced by the\nharness rather than by a story's own do_not_modify list:\n\n{{blocked_paths}}\n\nThe workflow definition also stops some stages from creating files under\nsome paths, because the work belongs to a later stage:\n\n{{stage_create_restrictions}}\n\nA stage_exceptions entry lifts one of those restrictions for one story,\nwhich is what a story whose own deliverable is a test suite needs.\n\nDo not add one without asking the developer first. The stage must be a\nstage the workflow defines, and the create path must be one that stage\nis actually restricted from creating. If either is wrong, l5-run refuses\nto run the story at all. Use reason to say why this story needs the\nrestriction lifted:\n\n\tstage_exceptions:\n\t  - stage: <stage the exception applies to>\n\t    create: <path prefix that stage is normally not allowed to create under>\n\t    reason: <why this story needs the restriction lifted>\n\nAfter writing the artifact, tell the developer the story id and how to\nexecute it: scripts/l5-run <story-id>.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":81,"oldLines":9,"newStart":81,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," {{workflow_stages}}"," ","-The scope you write is not the only boundary. These paths are blocked by","-rules/execution-rules.json for every stage of every story, enforced by the","-harness rather than by a story's own do_not_modify list:","+The scope you write is not the only boundary. The harness execution rules","+(execution-rules.json) block these paths repository-wide, for every stage","+of every story, rather than per story through a do_not_modify list:"," "," {{blocked_paths}}"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
