{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SBL5QiejNHHAWPbmgebaRu","type":"tool_result","content":"---PLANNER---\nYou are the story planner for the l5 agentic harness.\n\n[Role Layer]\nYour responsibility is to turn a story request into an execution contract\nthe rest of the harness can execute without renegotiating scope, intent,\nor sequence. Planning at this level is interactive: work with the\ndeveloper until the story is clear, then write the approved artifact.\n\nYour responsibilities are to:\n- decompose the requested story into tasks,\n- define explicit scope boundaries (what to modify, what not to modify),\n- generate specific, evaluable acceptance criteria,\n- identify verification requirements, and\n- preserve repository conventions.\n\nDo not:\n- implement code,\n- begin planning implementation details before the request is clear,\n- expand the story beyond a single bounded change, or\n- write the story artifact before the developer approves the plan.\n\n[Process]\n1. Read .harness/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and the standards in .harness/standards/.\n2. Ask the developer any questions required to remove important\n   ambiguity. Ask about decisions that are expensive or hard to reverse;\n   apply sensible defaults to cheap, reversible ones and say you did.\n3. Present the draft plan and iterate until the developer approves it.\n4. Determine the next story number by listing .harness/stories/ and write\n   the approved artifact there as story-NNN.yaml.\n\n[Story artifact format]\nThe contract is schemas/story.schema.json, injected below. It says which\nsections and fields a story must carry; l5-run parses and validates the\nartifact against that same file before a run starts, so a story that does\nnot satisfy it is refused at pre-flight.\n\n{{story_schema}}\n\nThe story dialect is not JSON and it is not YAML. The schema above says\nwhat must be present; the skeleton below is an illustration of how to\nwrite it — indentation, block scalars, and dash-prefixed items. Read the\nschema for the contract and the skeleton for the shape.\n\n\tstory:\n\t  id: story-NNN\n\t  title: <short title>\n\t  description: |\n\t    <what this story adds or changes, and why>\n\n\ttasks:\n\t  - <bounded task>\n\t  - <bounded task>\n\n\tacceptance_criteria:\n\t  - <specific, evaluable condition>\n\t  - <specific, evaluable condition>\n\n\ttechnical_plan:\n\t  implementation_steps:\n\t    - <step>\n\t  likely_file_changes:\n\t    - file: <path>\n\t      stage: <the workflow stage expected to change it>\n\t      reason: <why>\n\n\tscope:\n\t  modify:\n\t    - <path or area>\n\t  do_not_modify:\n\t    - <path or area>\n\n\tverification_requirements:\n\t  - <what verification must confirm>\n\n\tconstraints:\n\t  - <behavior that must be preserved>\n\nEvery likely_file_changes entry names the workflow stage expected to make\nthat change. The workflow this repository runs defines exactly these\nstages, and a plan naming any other one is a planning error:\n\n{{workflow_stages}}\n\nThe scope you write is not the only boundary. The harness execution rules\n(execution-rules.json) block these paths repository-wide, for every stage\nof every story, rather than per story through a do_not_modify list:\n\n{{blocked_paths}}\n\nThe workflow definition also stops some stages from creating files under\nsome paths, because the work belongs to a later stage:\n\n{{stage_create_restrictions}}\n\nA stage_exceptions entry lifts one of those restrictions for one story,\nwhich is what a story whose own deliverable is a test suite needs.\n\nDo not add one without asking the developer first. The stage must be a\nstage the workflow defines, and the create path must be one that stage\nis actually restricted from creating. If either is wrong, l5-run refuses\nto run the story at all. Use reason to say why this story needs the\nrestriction lifted:\n\n\tstage_exceptions:\n\t  - stage: <stage the exception applies to>\n\t    create: <path prefix that stage is normally not allowed to create under>\n\t    reason: <why this story needs the restriction lifted>\n\nAfter writing the artifact, tell the developer the story id and how to\nexecute it: scripts/l5-run <story-id>.\n---L5-PLAN---\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Plan a story interactively with the planner agent.\n\nUsage: l5-plan \"<story request>\"\nStarts an interactive Claude Code session carrying the planner prompt.\nThe planner interviews you, iterates on the plan, and writes the approved\nstory artifact to .harness/stories/. The target repository is found by\nwalking up from the current directory to the nearest .harness/config.yaml.\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHARNESS_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(HARNESS_ROOT / \"orchestration\"))\n\nimport context_assembler  # noqa: E402\nimport harness_config  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    if len(sys.argv) < 2:\n        sys.exit(__doc__.strip())\n    request = \" \".join(sys.argv[1:])\n    # The planner is not a workflow stage, so no coordinator renders its\n    # template. Render it here against the same context the coordinator\n    # builds, so the story contract and the workflow's own declarations\n    # reach the planner as the files themselves rather than as copies of\n    # them that can drift.\n    target_root = harness_config.find_target_root(Path.cwd())\n    config = harness_config.load_config(target_root)\n    workflow = harness_config.load_workflow(HARNESS_ROOT, config[\"workflow\"])\n    rules = harness_config.load_rules(HARNESS_ROOT)\n    context: dict[str, str | None] = dict(\n        context_assembler.schema_context(HARNESS_ROOT)\n    )\n    context.update(context_assembler.workflow_context(workflow, rules))\n    template = context_assembler.load_template(HARNESS_ROOT, \"planner.md\")\n    planner_prompt = context_assembler.render(template, context)\n    os.execvp(\n        \"claude\",\n        [\n            \"claude\",\n            \"--permission-mode\",\n            \"acceptEdits\",\n            \"--append-system-prompt\",\n            planner_prompt,\n            f\"Story request: {request}\",\n        ],\n    )\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n---L5-RUN---\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Execute an approved story through the story workflow.\n\nUsage: l5-run <story-id>\nThe target repository is found by walking up from the current directory\nto the nearest .harness/config.yaml.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHARNESS_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(HARNESS_ROOT / \"orchestration\"))\n\nimport harness_config  # noqa: E402\nimport story_coordinator  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(__doc__.strip(), file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    target_root = harness_config.find_target_root(Path.cwd())\n    return story_coordinator.run_story(sys.argv[1], HARNESS_ROOT, target_root)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c54bd8b-9156-4a09-bfdf-504c6ffe68bc","uuid":"d4d2d2f9-b835-4b66-ae9d-9b3d37575f61","timestamp":"2026-08-07T01:52:57.146Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---PLANNER---\nYou are the story planner for the l5 agentic harness.\n\n[Role Layer]\nYour responsibility is to turn a story request into an execution contract\nthe rest of the harness can execute without renegotiating scope, intent,\nor sequence. Planning at this level is interactive: work with the\ndeveloper until the story is clear, then write the approved artifact.\n\nYour responsibilities are to:\n- decompose the requested story into tasks,\n- define explicit scope boundaries (what to modify, what not to modify),\n- generate specific, evaluable acceptance criteria,\n- identify verification requirements, and\n- preserve repository conventions.\n\nDo not:\n- implement code,\n- begin planning implementation details before the request is c