{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdnZC89zsZtk8oZENaEmz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Verdict: **failed** — one blocking issue, retry not recommended\n\nWrote `.harness/runs/story-009/verification-result.json`. No `retry-guidance.json` (retry not recommended — see below).\n\n### What passes (verified from a fresh process)\n\n- **Injection is real, and the negative control proves it.** Rendering `prompts/planner.md` against this repo's workflow and rules yields all four stages (`implementer`, `tester`, `verifier`, `documenter`), the `tests/` prefix, and all three blocked paths (`.git/`, `.harness/runs/`, `rules/`), with zero leftover `{{placeholder}}`. Stripping the three new placeholders drops `tester`, `documenter` and all three blocked paths — coverage collapses. Separately, the *raw* template contains none of the four stage names and not `tests/`, so the three survivors of the strip (`implementer`, `verifier`, `tests/`) come from the injected `{{story_schema}}`, not prose.\n- **`find_target_root`** is in `orchestration/harness_config.py:13-23`, called from `scripts/l5-run:22` and `scripts/l5-plan:29`.\n- **`l5-plan`** exits non-zero with the no-config message and never reaches `execvp` (test uses a fake `claude` on PATH and asserts it was not invoked).\n- **`l5-run` is byte-for-byte unchanged** — the tester materializes `git show HEAD:scripts/l5-run` and compares returncode and stderr on both the no-config and usage paths.\n- `workflows/`, `rules/`, `schemas/` and `.harness/` are untouched (`git diff --stat HEAD` empty); 56 artifact-parsing tests pass; `build_context`'s `blocked_paths` change is behavior-preserving (empty list renders `'None'` either way).\n- The tester's edits to the story-007 and story-008 tests widen an allowlist and replace one assertion that this story deliberately reverses — both are story-sanctioned, not weakened assertions.\n\n### The blocking issue\n\n`.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q` → **1 failed, 321 passed**. The failure is `test_the_walk_up_loop_appears_once_in_the_repository`: the walk-up loop exists twice — `orchestration/harness_config.py:19-23` and `scripts/l5-status:19-23`, identical bodies and identical exit message (`grep` returns exactly those two hits).\n\nThis is a conflict inside the story, not an implementer error. `scripts/l5-status` is on `do_not_modify`, so no in-scope edit can satisfy \"the walk-up loop appears once in the repository.\" The implementer flagged it instead of editing a forbidden file; the tester asserted the criterion as written instead of softening it. Both did the right thing.\n\n**Retry not recommended** — a bounded retry cannot clear this within its authorized scope. It needs a developer decision: either authorize `scripts/l5-status` (one line, points it at `harness_config.find_target_root`) or narrow the criterion to \"the loop appears once outside `l5-status`\" and update the test to match.\n\nOne item is unverified: whether `tests/test_story_009_validation.py` was authored by the tester can't be confirmed from git (the file is untracked). The implementer's changed-files record lists nothing under `tests/`, and the working tree matches both records, so the evidence is consistent — but it's inference, not direct confirmation.\n\nI removed a temporary probe script I had written into the run directory; only `verification-result.json` remains from this stage."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2929,"cache_read_input_tokens":50618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2929},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c54bd8b-9156-4a09-bfdf-504c6ffe68bc","uuid":"8d322f3e-b581-4821-b868-27d6864699bc","timestamp":"2026-08-07T01:55:38.996Z","reques